Package: com.anlai.omnispeed
Name: OmniSpeed
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: Your speed and the road's speed limit, big on the iPhone screen.
 Prop your iPhone on the dash and OmniSpeed turns it into a speed display:
 your GPS speed in large digits, the speed limit of the road you are on as a
 road sign, and the road's name. Limits come from OpenStreetMap, so it works
 on any road the community has mapped - no navigation app needed.
 .
 Features:
  - GPS speed in large, easy-to-read digits
  - Speed limit sign for the road you are driving on, from OpenStreetMap
  - Road name under the speed
  - Red digits and a flashing frame when you go over the limit
  - Adjustable warning threshold, from 10 km/h under to 10 km/h over
  - Roads are downloaded once and kept on the phone for 30 days
  - Screen stays awake; portrait and landscape
 .
 Set it up in Settings > OmniSpeed. Needs location access and an internet
 connection the first time you drive a road.
 .
 Compatibility: iOS 15 and later, rootless jailbreaks (Dopamine, palera1n).
Icon: file:///var/jb/Library/PreferenceBundles/OmniSpeedPrefs.bundle/PackageIcon.png
Maintainer: AnLai <laihoangan123456@gmail.com>
Author: AnLai <laihoangan123456@gmail.com>
Section: Applications
Depends: preferenceloader, firmware (>= 15.0)
